ion several  months ago we just stepped that up and  we're looking for information about  other non-governmental organizations  that are doing just the same so this is  just the beginning we're going to try  try that angle to see if there's a way  that we can at least inhibit some of  these these non-government entities from  doing illegal work for the federal  government or for whoever  so Mr attorney general I'd love to ask  you one follow-up to Pete's question  about the tools at your disposal and I  want to say I think I speak for all of  us when we really appreciate you coming  on and answering these questions and I  think we're all on the same side of  hoping to solve what seems to be an  impossible or maybe not impossible an  unwilling issue of the federal  government to solve and that is this a  few a few weeks ago a month ago  um you got in texts that you declared  the governor put US declaration of an  invasion uh availing new powers in his  statement for the state to deport  illegal immigrants to the Border it was  criticized by some like uh Ken  cuccinelli who said there's no point in  taking somebody to the Border you have  to take somebody across the border for  it to be effective what I would love to  ask you today is a response to that and  B have you seen any appreciable effect  after you declared that invasion in  helping this crisis  yeah and it goes back to the the  challenge that I talked about most of  the people are not trying to evade  border patrol they're going directly to  border patrol so the idea of declaring  an evasion is is it's it's a fact I mean  it is an invasion and it should give us  the authority to do more we have two  challenges one the fact that they're  bringing people to the Border but  they're bringing to border patrol which  takes us out of the equation and second  we still have this Supreme Court  decision Arizona V U.S that was decided  under the Obama Administration that said  the federal government had complete  contr